    A013["<div class='arg'><b>A013 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>Warsh in the presser is more Warsh as at Jackson Hole than Warsh as at the July FOMC.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh's Jackson Hole-style presser is largely to support the bond.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A014["<div class='arg'><b>A014 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>Warsh's hawkish hike supports twist flattening of the UST curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A011 - PREDICTION</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A015 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A016 - FORECAST</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> The hawkish hike challenges the author's prior bias for lower belly rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> <b>A018 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>A017 - FORECAST</b></span></div></div>"]
    A015["<div class='arg'><b>A015 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>Warsh's hawkish hike supports higher front end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>P:</b> The hawkish presser sees 2Y rates rise 5-10bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The market raises the hike peak.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The market pulls forward hike timing.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh continues to sound inflation impatient.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh suggests recent data does not imply an adequate disinflation trend.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A016["<div class='arg'><b>A016 · FORECAST</b><div class='core fc'><span>The hawkish presser sees 30Y rates lower by 5-10bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are lower due to downside growth risk.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are lower due to downside inflation risk.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are lower due to a more credible Fed return to orthodoxy.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A017["<div class='arg'><b>A017 · FORECAST</b><div class='core fc'><span>The dovish presser sees 30Y rates higher by 5bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The market reduces the hike peak.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are higher due to dovish Fed action.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are higher due to confusion about Warsh policy direction or reaction function.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh implies an unpopular hike.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh implies few hikes to follow.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh implies improved signs in the inflation trend.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A018["<div class='arg'><b>A018 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The hawkish hike supports the author's constructive long end asset swap spread view.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Lower growth risk supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Lower inflation risk supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Enhanced Fed credibility supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A019["<div class='arg'><b>A019 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>The Fed delivers an additional rate hike in October.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Incoming data soften materially.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Fed communication turns unexpectedly dovish.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>Q:</b> Beyond next week's meeting, uncertainty around the policy path remains.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>IM:</b> The Fed delivers an additional rate hike in December.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A020["<div class='arg'><b>A020 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>Trump understands the risks of bond un-anchoring.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The Trump admin's choice is between tolerating modestly higher front end rates and materially higher long end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Bessent effectively explains to Trump the tradeoff between tolerating modestly higher front end rates and materially higher long end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh effectively explains to Trump the tradeoff between tolerating modestly higher front end rates and materially higher long end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The Trump admin understands bond risk with a Sept hold.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>CN:</b> Trump does not like the choice set between tolerating modestly higher front end rates and materially higher long end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A021["<div class='arg'><b>A021 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>In responding to questions about the policy path going forward, Warsh faces a balancing act.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>P:</b> Markets quickly price in over 100bp of hikes.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Markets once again question the Fed's commitment to the 2% inflation target.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh asserts that the Sep hike was the first in a sequence of rate increases.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh attempts a #quot;dovish hike#quot; by reassuring markets that the Fed will proceed cautiously.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A022["<div class='arg'><b>A022 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD outcome is determined by the Fed's ability to #quot;out-hawk#quot; market expectations and other G10 central banks.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A023 - FORECAST</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A025 - VIEW</b></span></div></div>"]
    A023["<div class='arg'><b>A023 · FORECAST</b><div class='core fc'><span>The USD trades more-or-less sideways into year-end (ex-JPY).</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A024 - VIEW</b></span></div></div>"]
    A024["<div class='arg'><b>A024 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The bar for the FOMC to #quot;out-hawk#quot; both expectations as well as other G10 central banks is high.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Part of the puzzle of the dollar being unable to rally amid the recent reacceleration in oil, gas, and refined energy products lies in the broader re-pricing of central banks and curves globally.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A025["<div class='arg'><b>A025 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>With evolving expectations, considerable two-way risk remains for the USD at Wednesday's meeting.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A026 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A027 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The dollar depreciates swiftly and significantly.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed opts to hold in the face of sticky inflation and market pricing.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A026["<div class='arg'><b>A026 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD is supported.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed hikes at least 100bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed brings current expectations forward.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>RI:</b> Chair Warsh's aversion to forward guidance makes the bullish USD case challenging.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh in the presser is as Warsh was at Jackson Hole.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed hikes.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The SEP shows broadening support for additional hikes (relative to the June SEP).</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Growth forecasts are elevated even in the context of further hike guidance.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Inflation forecasts are elevated even in the context of further hike guidance.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Chair Warsh himself, intentionally or unintentionally, offers some indication that a more prolonged campaign is necessary to return inflation on the path to 2%.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A027["<div class='arg'><b>A027 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD softens with dovish or non-committal language from Warsh.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Markets do not have the patience for anything that sounds like a #quot;one and done#quot; type event under the veil of #quot;no forward guidance#quot;.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The USD falls in tandem with rising back-end yields.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> A more restrained SEP dot-plot weighs on the dollar.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed hikes.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Messaging muddles the reaction function further.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Messaging that muddles the reaction function results in rising back-end yields.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The broader committee (outside of the already identified hawkish members) appears reluctant to tighten policy in the current environment.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]

